OpenTalk's patch to miniaudio 0.11.25 (dr_wav): refuse a "fmt " chunk whose size is smaller
than what was already read, or too large to seek over, instead of seeking backwards and
re-reading chunks forever. Found by fuzzing (tests/fuzz/fuzz_media_decoder); regression test:
tst_media_file, refusesAWavFileThatWouldHang. Recorded in docs/licensing/third-party-register.md.
Apply after opentalk-flac-seek.patch:
    patch -p1 -d third_party/miniaudio < third_party/miniaudio/opentalk-wav-fmt-chunk.patch

--- a/miniaudio.h
+++ b/miniaudio.h
@@ -81408,6 +81408,12 @@
                     cursor += fmt.extendedSize;
                     bytesReadSoFar += fmt.extendedSize;
                 }
+                /* OpenTalk patch (see third_party/miniaudio/opentalk-wav-fmt-chunk.patch): a chunk size
+                   smaller than what was read, or too large for an int, made this seek go backwards and
+                   the chunk loop never end (found by fuzzing). Such a file is damaged. */
+                if (header.sizeInBytes < (ma_uint64)bytesReadSoFar || header.sizeInBytes - (ma_uint64)bytesReadSoFar > 0x7FFFFFFF) {
+                    return MA_FALSE;
+                }
                 if (pWav->onSeek(pWav->pUserData, (int)(header.sizeInBytes - bytesReadSoFar), MA_DR_WAV_SEEK_CUR) == MA_FALSE) {
                     return MA_FALSE;
                 }
